 {"id":"fabro-d5a6","title":"web: files tab refuses large diffs ('too large to render inline') — offer truncated/per-record rendering","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T07:56:35.110Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T07:56:35.110Z","description":"User report 2026-09-05: in a run's Files tab, the diff for .seeds/issues.jsonl (182 records / ~264KB) is refused with '.seeds/issues.jsonl too large to render inline', so revisor-filed seeds cannot be reviewed in the UI at all. Wanted: at minimum a truncated diff with explicit cut + full-diff download; ideally per-record (JSONL line) diff rendering so one revisor cycle's additions are readable. Basis: revisor run on denkhaus, Files tab, 2026-09-05.","labels":["web","ux"]}
 {"id":"fabro-71b9","title":"web: kanban run tiles — show run date, workflow name, and workflow version","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-05T08:41:02.820Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-05T08:41:02.820Z","description":"User request 2026-09-05: the kanban run tiles currently show only title, diff status, repo, and PR numbers. Wanted additionally on each tile: (1) the run date (created_at or last activity), (2) the workflow name, (3) the workflow version. The workflow_version_id is content-derived (SHA-256 of the canonical workflow package) and exposed by the API run record as workflow.workflow_version_id (runs list since ADR-0015 engine change, 2026-09-05); render a short form (first ~12 hex chars) so tiles stay compact. Complements fabro-d5a6 (large-diff rendering); together they close the run-identity visibility gap in the UI.","labels":["web","ux","workflows"]}
